            "title": "Stellantis' shares tumble after posting modest gains, warning of future charges",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "Stellantis' shares dropped 10% on Thursday after the world's fourth-largest carmaker posted modest third-quarter gains and warned about possible future charges.  The Italian-French-U.S. carmaker that makes Jeep, Fiat and Peugeot vehicles reported a 13% increase in net revenues in the three months ending in September to 37.2 billion euros ($43.2 billion), ending seven quarters of decline on strong North American results as the carmaker showed the first signs of a turnaround under the new CEO.  Stellantis said that shipments rose 13% to 1.3 million vehicles, driven by North America, where it relaunched the popular HEMI V-8-powered RAM 1500 that had been nixed by previous management.",
